From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:44:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] technology: leaving offline mode must not depend on every
 technology

__connman_technology_set_offlinemode() switches every technology and
then decides by the result of the last one alone whether the new mode
stands. If that one failed, it read the previous mode back from the
settings file, although every technology before it had been switched
already.

On a MediaTek phone with GRE support in the kernel, the fallback
gretap0 and erspan0 devices are Ethernet devices with an all-zero
address, and enabling them fails with EADDRNOTAVAIL. With WiFi off when
offline mode was entered, Wired was the last technology to bring back,
so leaving offline mode turned cellular back on but left OfflineMode
true, saved as such, and never told the notifier. The shell reads
OfflineMode and kept showing airplane mode, and every further attempt
to leave it went the same way. The D-Bus caller got no error either,
since manager.c does not look at the result.

Leaving offline mode now always stands: a technology that cannot be
powered shows that in its own Powered property. Entering it is undone
only when no technology at all could be powered down, rather than when
the last one could not. A change that did take effect returns 0, where
leaving offline mode with no technology to bring back used to return
-EINVAL.

unit/test-offlinemode builds technology.c with the core stubbed and
covers leaving with the last, the first or the only technology failing
and with none to bring back, and entering with one or all of them
failing to go down.

Seen on a Q25 after turning airplane mode off from the system menu.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 Makefile.am             |  10 ++
 src/technology.c        |  23 ++-
 unit/test-offlinemode.c | 356 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 384 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 unit/test-offlinemode.c

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index 5b96ed0..4e7ac37 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -629,3 +629,13 @@ unit_test_ofono_LDADD = gdbus/libgdbus-internal.la \
 				@GLIB_LIBS@ @DBUS_LIBS@ -ldl
 
 TESTS += unit/test-ofono
+
+# Offline mode in the technology core, compiled into its test the same way.
+noinst_PROGRAMS += unit/test-offlinemode
+
+unit_test_offlinemode_SOURCES = $(backtrace_sources) src/log.c \
+				unit/test-offlinemode.c
+unit_test_offlinemode_LDADD = gdbus/libgdbus-internal.la \
+				@GLIB_LIBS@ @DBUS_LIBS@ -ldl
+
+TESTS += unit/test-offlinemode
diff --git a/src/technology.c b/src/technology.c
index ff1f0d5..2d17505 100644
--- a/src/technology.c
+++ b/src/technology.c
@@ -1896,6 +1896,7 @@ int __connman_technology_set_offlinemode(bool offlinemode)
 {
 	GSList *list;
 	int err = -EINVAL, enabled_tech_count = 0;
+	bool switched = false;
 
 	if (global_offlinemode == offlinemode)
 		return 0;
@@ -1917,9 +1918,11 @@ int __connman_technology_set_offlinemode(bool offlinemode)
 	for (list = technology_list; list; list = list->next) {
 		struct connman_technology *technology = list->data;
 
-		if (offlinemode)
+		if (offlinemode) {
 			err = technology_disable(technology);
-		else {
+			if (err == 0 || err == -EINPROGRESS || err == -EALREADY)
+				switched = true;
+		} else {
 			if (technology->hardblocked)
 				continue;
 
@@ -1930,12 +1933,22 @@ int __connman_technology_set_offlinemode(bool offlinemode)
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (err == 0 || err == -EINPROGRESS || err == -EALREADY ||
+	/*
+	 * Leaving offline mode always stands. A technology that cannot be
+	 * powered shows that in its own Powered property; putting offline
+	 * mode back for it left the others powered, as they had been enabled
+	 * already, under an OfflineMode that said they were not, and the
+	 * next attempt to leave it failed the same way. Entering offline
+	 * mode is undone only when no technology could be powered down.
+	 */
+	if (!offlinemode || switched ||
 			(err == -EINVAL && enabled_tech_count == 0)) {
 		connman_technology_save_offlinemode();
 		__connman_notifier_offlinemode(offlinemode);
-	} else
-		global_offlinemode = connman_technology_load_offlinemode();
+		return 0;
+	}
+
+	global_offlinemode = connman_technology_load_offlinemode();
 
 	return err;
 }
diff --git a/unit/test-offlinemode.c b/unit/test-offlinemode.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..70507a0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/unit/test-offlinemode.c
@@ -0,0 +1,356 @@
+/*
+ *
